{
  "_doc": "How outfit items (tools/blender/outfits.py) sit on each character. Items are modelled once on a canonical figure; per character, each anchor gives where that canonical frame goes (p) and how it stretches (s, per axis). head/eyes are in the head's frame (rig.head), neck/body in the body's (rig.pose), held in the right hand's (rig.handR); a character that lists no anchor for a slot uses the canonical one. 'hide' lists items that cannot fit a character (its own hat, helmet or visor is in the way); 'items' nudges one item on one character on top of its anchor (p adds, s multiplies). 'neckOverBody' widens the neck item when a body item is also worn, so it sits over the collar. 'mane' picks, per character whose mane is a node of its own (the Chog: chog_Hair_<cut> in its model, tools/blender/characters.py MANES), the cut of it worn under each head item, so some spikes always show without poking through the hat (the whole mane otherwise).",
